<Project Sdk="Microsoft.NET.Sdk">

  <!--
    Functionally like anyunit-runner (Runner/Platforms/net10 + shared),
    but deliberately narrower: it only ever discovers/runs tests in the
    CALLING assembly (Assembly.GetCallingAssembly() - whichever assembly's
    own entry point invoked this), never an arbitrary list of external
    .dll paths the way anyunit-runner's own CLI takes them. No ManyConsole/
    argument parsing, no "point this at any .dll" support - just a static
    method a consumer's own entry point calls directly, in place of a
    generated/hand-rolled Main:

      [<EntryPoint>]
      let main _ = AnyUnit.Runner.Bootstrap.Runner.Run("net10")

    This is the library form of the pattern hand-rolled this session for
    both QrLinkPdf.Tests.fsproj's own desktop Program.fs (AnyUnit.
    TestingPlatform's own EnableAnyUnitRunner codegen is C#-only, so an
    .fsproj needs its own hand-written MTP entry point) and
    QrLinkPdf.Tests.Wasm's Program.fs (a plain console entry point run
    under node/bun, no Blazor hosting/headless browser needed - see
    Runner/Platforms/browser-wasm-runner-host/Readme.md) - formalized so
    neither of those needs to hand-roll Runner.Create/RunAll and its own
    console-output formatting again.

    netstandard2.0 (not a specific TFM): needs to work under whichever
    host actually calls it - desktop CLR, Mono/browser-wasm interpreter,
    or (should AnyUnit ever add it) WASI - same reasoning as AnyUnit's own
    core libraries.

    Lives under Runner/ (not the repo root) alongside Platforms/net10 and
    Platforms/browser-wasm-runner - a third runner flavor (library-
    embedded rather than a standalone CLI or wasm host), not core. Its
    own console/TeamCity output formatting is Platforms/shared's own
    PrintTests.cs, Compile-Included directly (not a ProjectReference -
    it's a single dependency-free file, and this project's own
    netstandard2.0 TFM can't reference net10-runner's net10.0 one
    anyway): that file has no ManyConsole dependency of its own (only
    Commands.cs/RunAloneCommand.cs/Program.cs there do, for the actual
    CLI argument parsing this project deliberately has none of) - real
    duplicate implementations of the exact same output format once
    existed here and in Platforms/shared before this, kept in sync only
    by hand.
  -->
  <PropertyGroup>
    <TargetFramework>netstandard2.0</TargetFramework>
    <IsPackable>true</IsPackable>
    <PackageId>AnyUnit.Runner.Bootstrap</PackageId>
    <Description>Static Runner.Run(platform) a consumer's own entry point calls directly - discovers/runs only the calling assembly's own tests, no CLI/argument parsing, no external-assembly support (see anyunit-runner for that).</Description>
    <PackageReadmeFile>README.md</PackageReadmeFile>
  </PropertyGroup>

  <ItemGroup>
    <ProjectReference Include="..\..\AnyUnit\AnyUnit.csproj" />
  </ItemGroup>

  <ItemGroup>
    <Compile Include="..\Platforms\shared\PrintTests.cs" Link="PrintTests.cs" />
  </ItemGroup>

  <ItemGroup>
    <None Include="README.md" Pack="true" PackagePath="\" />
  </ItemGroup>

</Project>
